  "body": "**Card:** `scope-navigation` (consolidation track, chooser seed `ef0afbea84ae0155fdc123ffbb7a0329`, base `49b3157d`). Scope unchanged. No new \u03ba.\n\n## The confusing path\n`docs/research/current-status.md` is linked from CONTRIBUTING and autoresearch as the place to read the current result. Below its real top section, it contains:\n- two more `# Current reviewed status` headings, under the #1042 snapshot (\u03ba 0.001672188\u2026) and the #942 snapshot (\u03ba 0.001661960\u2026);\n- `# Selected construction: \u2026` (\u03ba 0.00066, #186);\n- `# Current contracts and research status` (2^-30, October 8), with `## Current and earlier results`, `## Exact current parameters and bottleneck` and `## Next research priority`. That last one says the next improvement \"should target the bit finite network\", but today the **complex** side binds.\n\nA reader or agent that searches or jumps by heading can land on any of these. Several research notes already warn that historical notes say \"current\" for obsolete checkpoints; this page is the most-linked instance.\n\n## Change\n- These seven headings are renamed to name their checkpoint (for example `## Reviewed status at the #1042 checkpoint` and `## Research priority at the 2^-31 integration (superseded; see autoresearch.md)`).\n- One banner is added where the history begins. It says that \"current/selected/latest/next\" inside historical sections refer to their own checkpoint, and points to `selected-result.json` and `autoresearch.md`.\n- **No section body is changed**, so the history is preserved verbatim.\n- New `tests/test_research_current_status.py`:\n  - only the first heading may say current, selected or next research;\n  - the top section must contain the selected record's `decimal`, review filename and `reproduce` command;\n  - the banner must be present.\n\n  The test **fails on main's text** (2 failures) and passes with this change. When the status page is next updated, the previous top heading must be demoted, which is exactly the step that was missed.\n\n## Checks\n- `python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests -p 'test_research_*.py'`: 23 OK, 1 skipped.\n- No links to the renamed anchors exist in the repository.\n- Three packages pin `current-status.md` (`u8-terminal-cone-census`, `e8-joint-reader-bound`, `r480-quad12-exact-seed12`). All pin older blobs as historical provenance, none of which match current main, so no live pin changes.\n- Overlap: `find_overlap.py 'current-status' 'current reviewed status' 'navigation'` found no open PR or discussion on this page. Open PR file lists were not searched exhaustively.\n\n**Feedback:** this is from the same contributor as #1228 and #1231. The friction from the first session was that \"current\" appears in many superseded headings.\n\nPrepared by Douglas Colkitt with Claude (Anthropic) assistance. Apache-2.0.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
